{"name":"Portobello Mushroom","hex":"#9d928a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"portobello","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The large, mature form of the crimini mushroom (Agaricus bisporus)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/portobello"},{"term":"mushroom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the fleshy fruiting bodies of fungi typically produced above ground on soil or on their food sources (such as decaying wood).","A fungus producing such fruiting bodies."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having characteristics like those of a mushroom, for example in shape or appearance, speed of growth, or texture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mushroom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Agaricus bisporus","blocks":[{"text":"Agaricus bisporus, the cultivated mushroom, is a basidiomycete mushroom native to grasslands in Eurasia and North America. It is cultivated in more than 70 countries and is one of the most commonly and widely consumed mushrooms in the world. It has two color states while immature – white and brown – both of which have various names, with additional names for the mature state, such as chestnut, portobello, portabellini, button, cremini, and champignon de Paris."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/ChampignonMushroom.jpg/330px-ChampignonMushroom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agaricus_bisporus","wikidata":"Q227690"},{"title":"Mushroom","blocks":[{"text":"A mushroom is the fleshy, spore-bearing fruiting body of a fungus, typically produced above ground on soil or another food source. A toadstool generally refers to a poisonous mushroom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Sparrige_Sch%C3%BCppling_%28Pholiota_squarrosa%29.jpg/330px-Sparrige_Sch%C3%BCppling_%28Pholiota_squarrosa%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_con